1
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,530
Kirito.

2
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,260
Yeah, Alne?

3
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,500
Listen, I have faith in
your skills as a swordsman,

4
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,140
but I have to warn you about something.

5
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,820
The Levantains have a saying,
handed down for generations.

6
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:43,017
Soak your sword in the
blood of the mighty,

7
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,982
and you will make their
strength become your own.

8
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,920
Like blood, blood? Yes.

9
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,740
Before he started here,

10
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:56,413
Volo had been engaging in first-strike
duels with real swords for a while.

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,441
As a result of that, those experiences
are what gave him his power.

12
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,220
His imagination, of course.

13
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:07,617
Volo's strength is tied to an
old family motto he grew up with.

14
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:12,560
So if he beats someone strong, he
believes he'll get stronger from it.

15
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,150
Watch out.

16
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:18,572
He aims to draw blood today so he can
wet his blade and grow even stronger.

17
00:01:21,780 --> 00:01:23,420
I know you can do this.

18
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,440
I have the utmost faith in you.

19
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:29,722
You are not the type of swordsman
who would fall so easily to him.

20
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:34,227
Also, this is the perfect
opportunity to fulfill your promise.

21
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,700
What promise?

22
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,533
Oh, yeah, I said I'd show you
the best sword skill I had.

23
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,040
That's right, so show
it to me here, on him.

24
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:45,990
Done.

25
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:47,544
You'll see the best one I know.

26
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,180
Shall we start, trainee Kirito?

27
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,170
Yeah.

28
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:05,040
Elite Disciple Surlute, will you
serve as witness to this duel?

29
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,320
Yes, of course.

30
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:13,980
Elite Disciple Leventain
versus Primary Trainee Kirito.

31
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:17,335
The victor shall be the one
who lands the first strike.

32
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:23,960
Let it be known that both parties have
agreed to use real swords in this match.

33
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:26,670
Let's go,

34
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:36,040
let's

35
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,270
go.

36
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:49,590
Is

37
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,060
hear sure

38
00:03:43,293 --> 00:03:44,123
Shining Summer Diamond

39
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:50,331
I'll be the same as the dream of the world

40
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:32,480
Oh my word, I didn't know painting
swords black was a custom in the boonies.

41
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:33,800
Did you, Lord Rios?

42
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,240
Don't be so insensitive, Umber.

43
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:41,326
It's not the poor Page's fault he's too
busy to polish the filth from his sword.

44
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,660
A mountain-splitting wave
of the High-Norkian style.

45
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,080
He's starting with his best skill.

46
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,500
That's Avalanche.

47
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:14,560
A heavy one-hit thrust.

48
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,780
But it's the hardcore version of it.

49
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:21,180
His imagination's boosting its power.

50
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,700
Dodging's not an option.

51
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,150
No.

52
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,420
I'm gonna have to block his strike.

53
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:30,700
I got a promise to keep.

54
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:34,220
I have to counter with something bigger.

55
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:37,140
Like the four-part vertical square.

56
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:08,180
He blocked it!

57
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:19,900
If I can hold out, I can
still get my fourth hidden!

58
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:26,160
Holy crap!

59
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:28,580
Is that the source of his power?

60
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:39,140
He's picturing his
ancestors, backing him up!

61
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,760
I won't lose to him.

62
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:48,100
No way!

63
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,660
I can't!

64
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:59,040
I'm not gonna let you beat me! Please!

65
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,172
Did his sword just grow?

66
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,960
That is enough!

67
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,720
Ms. Zazurka...

68
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:02,680
If she decides the duel
is over, we must obey her.

69
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:05,710
Um, okay.

70
00:08:05,793 --> 00:08:06,900
But why, though?

71
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:08,370
Years ago,

72
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:11,420
during the Four Empire
Unification Tournament,

73
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:15,251
she was the first swordsman to
represent North Norlingarth.

74
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:19,580
Trainee Kirito's punishment
is hereby fulfilled!

75
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,940
Next time, try not to
fling mud onto anyone.

76
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,560
You were lucky today.

77
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:49,200
It's back to normal.

78
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:56,720
I thought you had been slashed.

79
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,360
Yeah.

80
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,314
Talk about close, huh?

81
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:02,939
Anyone else would have surrendered.

82
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:04,860
Oh, you hopeless fool.

83
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:12,340
That said, it was a
magnificent fight. Well done.

84
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,900
I am forever grateful.

85
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:18,844
On the one hand, I wish
I could have fought you.

86
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:24,362
But on the other, you did keep your promise
and showed me what you were capable of.

87
00:09:24,660 --> 00:09:25,490
Nicely done.

88
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:28,680
But, um, nobody won. It was a draw.

89
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:33,560
Is achieving a draw against the first
seat not good enough for you? Uh, no.

90
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:36,140
That's not what I meant. I hope not.

91
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:37,997
The result wasn't even the point.

92
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,877
Seeing you fight was, actually.

93
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:41,313
It taught me something.

94
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:43,785
Something extremely important.

95
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:48,173
We can talk about it back at
my place while we celebrate.

96
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,540
We'll invite Eugeo and
Lord Golgorosso, too.

97
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,630
Sure.

98
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,120
Hmm.

99
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,297
attacks are so diverse.

100
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:32,968
In my book, that's what
makes it so amazing.

101
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,500
It's history as two. How?

102
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:43,557
Once, a distant ancestor of mine
angered the Emperor at the time,

103
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,717
and because of that,

104
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:49,447
the Sir Lute family was banished from
the official Hynorkia style indefinitely.

105
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:50,650
Oh.

106
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:54,480
So my family improvised,
and then from that,

107
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,993
our non-traditional style was developed,

108
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:58,880
becoming the Sir Lute style.

109
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:01,360
I don't resent it by any means.

110
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:04,975
On the contrary, I have always
been proud of our style.

111
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:10,200
Still, I may have retained some
doubts about its legitimacy.

112
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,120
These two years,

113
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:17,341
I couldn't beat Volo, not because
he specialized in a better style,

114
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:19,560
but because I felt mine was lesser.

115
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,150
Lina.

116
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,920
You and I, though, we both have
unique styles of swordplay.

117
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:31,601
The difference is, you don't feel inferior
to those trained in more orthodox styles.

118
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:35,060
After watching you this past year,

119
00:11:35,300 --> 00:11:38,720
and seeing how you fought
with Volo in today's duel,

120
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,980
to be honest, I think I
understand why you don't.

121
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:43,420
For me,

122
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:48,860
knowing I'm the successor to the Surludes'
style fills me with great pride and joy.

123
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,828
There is no better feeling.

124
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:54,565
Becoming your mentor is
a close second, though.

125
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:56,817
Thanks, Lina.

126
00:11:56,900 --> 00:11:59,277
And now that you saw how I countered Volo,

127
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:03,360
you shouldn't have any trouble
beating him in the finals. Right.

128
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:27,100
Oh, well, well, what perfect timing.

129
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:31,420
I was hoping I'd run into
you, and here you are.

130
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:33,500
What do you guys want?

131
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:39,708
Well, naturally, I wanted to commend you
on your dazzling performance earlier.

132
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:43,080
True, those were some very
flashy-looking skills.

133
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:48,080
I'm certain you unnerved first-seat
Leventayne with your dashing theatrics.

134
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,677
Would you pick in a fight?

135
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:53,140
Certainly not.

136
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:57,657
A nobleman would never dare engage in
uncouth activities with a commoner.

137
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:59,640
Unless it's giving handouts.

138
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,700
To praise your stunt.

139
00:13:06,940 --> 00:13:09,960
No, to honor your battle. Here is a gift.

140
00:13:10,180 --> 00:13:11,380
No need to thank me.

141
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,820
It is my one charitable act for the day.

142
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:16,920
Good night, Sir Kirito.

143
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,340
Sir nothing!

144
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:51,260
It started out as an experiment.

145
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:59,421
The Zephelia is a type of flower that doesn't
bloom anywhere in the Northern Empire.

146
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:02,072
Lena told me that they were her favorite.

147
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:06,580
I tried to make them bloom,
using my imagination theory.

148
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:12,260
And along the way, I started
identifying with the flowers,

149
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,820
because I knew how hard it was

150
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,773
trying to stay alive in a foreign place.

151
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:23,817
Having been cut off from the real world
and all the people I loved and cared for.

152
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:27,597
Made me feel more and more
alone as time went on here.

153
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:30,440
I shared that pain with these flowers.

154
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,080
I'm sorry.

155
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,560
Have faith.

156
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:02,417
Believe in the strength of the flowers.

157
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:04,197
You grew in this foreign soil.

158
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,337
Who's there?

159
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:07,717
Believe in yourself too.

160
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,860
For helping them grow
as well as they have.

161
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:14,050
Yeah.

162
00:15:14,133 --> 00:15:16,820
But it didn't matter in the end.

163
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:18,680
Worry not.

164
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:22,100
Their roots still cling
to life within the soil.

165
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,980
You sense it, do you not?

166
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:29,580
The sacred flowers in this garden
want to save their friends.

167
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,900
Their energy shall aid you.

168
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:36,397
But how?

169
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:39,160
I don't know any of the
spells that can help.

170
00:15:39,920 --> 00:15:41,500
You do not need to.

171
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:45,357
The arts are only tools to
harness and refine the meaning,

172
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:48,180
or what you call the mental image.

173
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:50,640
Use your heart.

174
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:55,060
Feel the prayers of the
flowers, the ways of the world.

175
00:15:56,440 --> 00:16:00,040
Feel the prayers of the
flowers, the meaning.

176
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:29,620
Please, help me.

177
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:32,600
I need you to share some of your power.

178
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:40,480
Imagine the flower's life force flowing
through you and into the Zephelia's roots.

179
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:13,900
Whoever you are,

180
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,380
Thanks a lot.

181
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,270
Let's go!

182
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:21,620
Ah!

183
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,150
Yeah!

184
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,000
Ah!

185
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:40,990
Ah!

186
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,600
Ah! Ah!

187
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:48,640
Match over!

188
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:12,071
Lena graduated from the North
Senator Swordcraft Academy.

189
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:16,780
She was the top-ranked student that year.

190
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,400
After our advancement exam,

191
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:24,437
Eugeo and me were ranked
seat five and six?

192
00:19:24,520 --> 00:19:27,080
and got promoted to elite disciples.

193
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:32,960
Elite disciple Eugeo, I am here to report.

194
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:36,560
The assigned cleaning has been completed.

195
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:38,540
Thanks, Tiese. Good work.

196
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:42,133
I don't have anything else
for you, so you're free to go.

197
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:46,500
Oh, and, um...

198
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,480
I'm sorry, Ronie.

199
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:53,657
I don't know how many times I've told him
to be back before you finish cleaning,

200
00:19:53,740 --> 00:19:54,975
but he never listens.

201
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:56,210
It's fine.

202
00:19:56,293 --> 00:19:59,477
I'll just wait until he comes
back so I can make my report.

203
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:01,217
You know, if you really want,

204
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:05,357
I can always put in a good word so you can
get your mentor changed to someone else.

205
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:08,657
You're going to have a really
long year if you serve under him.

206
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:09,570
Just a warning.

207
00:20:09,653 --> 00:20:12,360
Oh, I don't mind. I knew it.

208
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:15,826
You guys were talking
about me behind my back.

209
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:21,220
Um, Elate Disciple
Kirito, here's my report.

210
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:22,835
Cleaning is complete.

211
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,917
Everything is shiny and spotless.

212
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,420
Oh, OK, thanks.

213
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:27,960
Come on, Kirito.

214
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:31,317
These two have a lot on their
plate, so please respect that.

215
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:34,377
At least try to get back here
before they're done cleaning.

216
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:37,717
And could you tell me why you're coming
in through the window all of a sudden?

217
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:40,617
Because it's the shortest
route from East 3rd Street.

218
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,137
It's way faster than
going through the lobby.

219
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:46,837
Keep that in mind, because on days
you're running late, it's a lifesaver.

220
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:47,780
Oh, right!

221
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:49,945
Could you not teach them that?

222
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:54,924
Hang on, if you're coming from
East 3rd, then that bag is from...

223
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:58,397
So much for manners when
your stomach's rumbling.

224
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,360
Eh, U-G-O?

225
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:01,730
Here.

226
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:09,660
Here, I bought extra so you can
share some with your doormates.

227
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,600
Thank you so much, Ely Disciple Kirito.

228
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:19,677
We'll head back as fast as we can and
eat these before their life decreases.

229
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:21,113
We'll see you tomorrow.

230
00:21:23,940 --> 00:21:26,677
It's full of honey pies
from the Prancing Deer Cafe.

231
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,701
Let's hurry before they get cold.

232
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:29,750
Come on.

233
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:33,950
What's up?

234
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,360
Oh, nothing much, really.

235
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,080
It's just, I'm wondering
where your head's at.

236
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,537
I hope you haven't gotten
so comfortable lately that

237
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:45,738
you've forgotten why we came
here in the first place.

238
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:47,020
Like I'd forget.

239
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,240
We're closer now than ever.

240
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:57,030
Mm-hmm.

241
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:01,060
Almost there.

242
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:38,800
Next time, Nobleman's Obligations.
